> **Before any UI work, read [`docs/design-language.md`](./docs/design-language.md)** —
> the full house language (bands, signal, type, motion, glyphs, contrast gate,
> banned list, and a self-check). It is deliberately not summarised here: this
> file loads every session, that one loads only when you touch UI.

The app follows the house **CodaSignal "Signal"** design language: full-bleed
bands that alternate dark (`#0e0f0d`) and light (`#f2f2ee`) with a quarter-width
ruled backdrop behind each, one chromatic signal in four temperatures (Jade is
the default) that only ever marks the second line of a heading, live data, or a
list number, fixed status colours that never theme (degraded `#c99a3a`, incident
`#c9553a`, idle = faint ink), Archivo at 600/500 with tight negative tracking for
everything readable, and JetBrains Mono for every label/tag/data/glyph/code line.
Depth is a hairline; a panel adds one soft shadow on a light band and none on a
dark one. No serif, no italic, no second hue, no gradients, no icon library.

**Hard rules:** no hardcoded hex or magic numbers in components — utilities only
(`bg-*`/`text-*`/`border-*` · `rounded-*` · `type-*` · `ease-signal` +
`duration-(--duration-*)` · `icons`/`glyphs`). The token stylesheets reset
Tailwind's stock scales to `initial`, so `text-sm`, `font-bold`, `rounded-2xl`,
`shadow-lg`, `ease-in-out` and the stock colour ramps do not exist here — that is
the ban being structural, not a class that failed to load. The signal never fills
a button. Focus is always visible: a 1px `border-accent` plus a 3px
`focus-ring` wash. Numbers in readouts are tabular (the `type-*` roles that carry
figures already set it). Hover changes colour or border in
`duration-(--duration-hover)` and never adds a shadow; press is `active:translate-y-px`.
Motion flattens under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. The band is a CSS-variable
seam: `:root` carries the dark band, `.band-light` overrides it, and the utilities
resolve through `var(--tone-*)` — so a component follows whichever band it lands
in, as long as it never hardcodes a value.

- **Deviations from the house language:** <none | what-and-why>

